# Build output. Regenerated by ./build.sh, and ~22MB per revision.
dist/

# Local build tooling, artefact backups and scratch work. work/fnpack holds the
# official fnpack binary; tools/build resolves it from PATH and prints the
# download URL when it is absent, so a fresh clone still builds after fetching
# fnpack. work/backup keeps old .fpk revisions only for demonstrating that
# `go run ./tools/fpk verify` rejects a stale package.
work/

# The bundled cloudflared binary: a 40MB third-party build that upstream already
# publishes. Tracking it would put it in every clone and in the permanent
# history, for a file nobody here edits. tools/fetchcf downloads the pinned
# release and verifies its SHA-256 before use; the packaged .fpk, which does
# contain the binary, ships as a GitHub Release asset.
cloudflared/app/bin/cloudflared

# The service binary is a build artefact too: tools/build cross-compiles it from
# cmd/fncfd (linux/amd64, CGO disabled) into the payload.
cloudflared/app/bin/fncfd

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Local Go toolchain, module/build caches and downloaded artefacts. Never
# committed: build.sh only falls back to .toolchain/go when `go` is not on PATH.
.toolchain/
repo.zip
